Thought: The proton shifts data confirms the presence of an alkyne group (2.0 - 3.2 ppm) and typical alkyl groups (methyl at ~0.9 ppm, methylene at ~1.3 ppm). The presence of a signal at 1.96 ppm (s, 1H) could be indicative of a terminal alkyne proton. The IR and NMR data suggest a compound with a terminal alkyne and an alkyl chain. I will now use the simulate_spectra tool to verify the structure by simulating the spectra for a potential SMILES string that fits this data.
